,0)$ with semi-axes of lengths $1$ and $25.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508686 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508686 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c127f29f-052a-5794-b5b2-3be574c6f2dd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508728 #edb/ref 1080 "An ellipse centered at $(-3,0)$ with semi-axes of lengths $1$ and $5.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508728 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508728 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d208bca8-3704-5c6a-88be-21b04308174b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508734 #edb/ref 1080 "The parabola $(y-4)^{2}=x+1$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508734 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508734 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d573fd0d-d62b-50c0-9361-ac2dddd6713c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508755 #edb/ref 1080 "\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\text{ }x-y>12\\}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508755 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508755 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e5818807-d65a-5f49-aebe-5e5a28895c19" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508785 #edb/ref 1080 "An ellipse centered at $(-3,0)$ with semi-axes of lengths $1$ and $\\sqrt{5}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508785 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508785 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f3b0ef1b-8d1b-5903-bf0c-073528025c0e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508842 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186508435 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508842 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186508508 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508842 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186508686 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508842 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186508728 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508842 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186508785 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508842 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508842 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508842 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186508728 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508842 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "61868b69-fdbd-5aff-bb91-accdf71cfa90" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508861 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186508505 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508861 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186508541 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508861 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186508556 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508861 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186508642 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508861 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186508734 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508861 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508861 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508861 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186508556 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508861 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "9738db51-6bb6-5a1e-9a88-9854819dcf8d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508918 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186508842 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508918 #edb/ref 1069 "q-164423" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508918 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508918 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the domain in the $xy$-plane of the elliptic cylinder $(x+3)^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}=1?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508918 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2ff3c43f-106f-5820-9db0-287d2d56d9d9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508918 #edb/ref 1074 "The full expression describing all points on our elliptic cylinder is\n\n$$\n(x+3)^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}=1,\\,z=k\n$$\n\nwhere $k\\in R$ can vary arbitrarily. \n\nThe domain of any cylinder in the $xy$-plane is its base curve. Hence, in this case, the domain is\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:(x+3)^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}=1\\}\n$$\n\nwhich can be written as\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{{1}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{5}^{2}}=1\\}.\n$$\n\nThis is an ellipse centered at $(-3,0)$ with semi-axes of lengths $1$ and $5.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508975 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186508861 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508975 #edb/ref 1069 "q-164404" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508975 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508975 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the trace in the $xy$-plane of the parabolic cylinder $(y-4)^{2}=z+1?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508975 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c57b9d4a-351a-58d6-893f-d761a9a6ee5e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508975 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the trace in the $xy$-plane, we substitute $z=0$ into the equation of the cylinder, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-4)^{2} & =0+1 \\\\ (y-4)^{2} & =1 \\\\ y-4 & =\\pm 1 \\\\ y & =4\\pm 1 \\\\ y & =3,5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of two lines $y=3$ and $y=5$ in the $xy$-plane." #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
